adjudication.rationale:
In EnableTwoFactorModal’s DisplayBackupCodes step, the Copy button handler calls `navigator.clipboard.writeText(...)` directly with no feature-detection or try/catch:
```ts
onClick={(e) => {
  e.preventDefault();
  navigator.clipboard.writeText(...);
  showToast(...);
}}
```
If `navigator.clipboard` is undefined (e.g., non-secure context) or the call rejects/throws, this will result in an unhandled error and can prevent the toast from showing; there is also no fallback copy mechanism. This is a real runtime failure mode introduced by the diff.
